		<article id="comment-759" class="comment">
			<header class="comment-meta comment-author vcard">
				<img referrerpolicy="no-referrer" alt='katster&#039;s avatar' src='https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/479cf054e2879644e03a0f478c7cdd06929f22a85b6cb68e35df69f6fcfe26d4?s=44&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G' srcset='https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/479cf054e2879644e03a0f478c7cdd06929f22a85b6cb68e35df69f6fcfe26d4?s=44&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 1x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/479cf054e2879644e03a0f478c7cdd06929f22a85b6cb68e35df69f6fcfe26d4?s=66&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 1.5x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/479cf054e2879644e03a0f478c7cdd06929f22a85b6cb68e35df69f6fcfe26d4?s=88&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 2x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/479cf054e2879644e03a0f478c7cdd06929f22a85b6cb68e35df69f6fcfe26d4?s=132&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 3x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/479cf054e2879644e03a0f478c7cdd06929f22a85b6cb68e35df69f6fcfe26d4?s=176&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 4x' class='avatar avatar-44' height='44' width='44' loading='lazy' decoding='async' /><cite><b class="fn"><a href="http://retstak.org" class="url" rel="ugc external nofollow">katster</a></b> </cite><a href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/#comment-759"><time datetime="2016-05-29T21:47:33+02:00">May 29, 2016 at 21:47</time></a>			</header><!-- .comment-meta -->

				
				
			<section class="comment-content comment">
				<p>Good interview, SFkitten!  It&#8217;s helpful for me as well to have something to compare the book against because I&#8217;ve not read Wolfe either.  I keep meaning to, and other things distract me.</p>
<p>I actually feel a bit bad for Aramini.  It sounds like he&#8217;s put his heart into this book, and that it&#8217;s decent work, on par with some of the finalists and winners in the category.  But because he&#8217;s published by Beale, and on Beale&#8217;s slate&#8230;  I&#8217;m not saying it&#8217;s fair, but he&#8217;s starting with two strikes, and he&#8217;s going to have to hit the ball well to get over that.</p>
<p>My personal heuristic is that anybody that advocates the destruction of the Hugo award, and Beale certainly counts as he&#8217;s said he wants to burn it to the ground, is immediately and automatically excluded from my ballot.  I&#8217;m having a tougher time deciding what to do about the folks associated with his publishing house.  Guess I&#8217;ll just keep reading and grapple with it if I find something that, in my opinion, would have gotten a nod on my ballot if not from Castalia.</p>
<p id="comment-like-759" data-liked=comment-not-liked class="comment-likes comment-not-liked"><a href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/?like_comment=759&#038;_wpnonce=3b24e42ba7" class="comment-like-link needs-login" rel="nofollow" data-blog="85585660"><span>Like</span></a><span id="comment-like-count-759" class="comment-like-feedback">Liked by <a href="#" class="view-likers" data-like-count="1">1 person</a></span></p>
							</section><!-- .comment-content -->

				<div class="reply">
