	<li class="comment byuser comment-author-markhepworthuk odd alt thread-odd thread-alt depth-1" id="li-comment-768">
		<article id="comment-768" class="comment">
			<header class="comment-meta comment-author vcard">
				<img referrerpolicy="no-referrer" alt='Mark Hepworth&#039;s avatar' src='https://2.gravatar.com/avatar/bc2b6cf4d1b82d574c2b84659612a1c7a86436580c6fe0c63091958b6132321a?s=44&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G' srcset='https://2.gravatar.com/avatar/bc2b6cf4d1b82d574c2b84659612a1c7a86436580c6fe0c63091958b6132321a?s=44&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 1x, https://2.gravatar.com/avatar/bc2b6cf4d1b82d574c2b84659612a1c7a86436580c6fe0c63091958b6132321a?s=66&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 1.5x, https://2.gravatar.com/avatar/bc2b6cf4d1b82d574c2b84659612a1c7a86436580c6fe0c63091958b6132321a?s=88&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 2x, https://2.gravatar.com/avatar/bc2b6cf4d1b82d574c2b84659612a1c7a86436580c6fe0c63091958b6132321a?s=132&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 3x, https://2.gravatar.com/avatar/bc2b6cf4d1b82d574c2b84659612a1c7a86436580c6fe0c63091958b6132321a?s=176&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 4x' class='avatar avatar-44' height='44' width='44' loading='lazy' decoding='async' /><cite><b class="fn"><a href="http://sfmmxv.wordpress.com" class="url" rel="ugc external nofollow">Mark</a></b> </cite><a href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/#comment-768"><time datetime="2016-05-30T01:59:37+02:00">May 30, 2016 at 01:59</time></a>			</header><!-- .comment-meta -->

				
				
			<section class="comment-content comment">
				<p>Very good interview, and it was interesting to hear more about how Aramini came to write this. I&#8217;d actually just been browsing through his book from the packet when I saw this, so it&#8217;s timely as well!</p>
<p>I&#8217;m nowhere close to having read enough Wolfe to judge Aramini&#8217;s scholarship, so I&#8217;m simply assuming it&#8217;s sound. What I did find with the various essays is that they seem to be very far down the rabbit hole of arguing with other scholars of Wolfe and so offered little to the general reader. Specialised interest is not necessarily a weakness of itself, but I was puzzled by the lack of any overarching analysis or conclusions. For example, there&#8217;s a meticulous series on his short work which details each story in turn, but there&#8217;s nothing analysing his works as a body. Equally, while the essays on the novels do necessarily broaden out to look at Wolfe&#8217;s work, they also seem to be jumping straight into existing arguments in studies of Wolfe without introduction. </p>
<p>For me this puts Aramini&#8217;s pleas that he couldn&#8217;t get it published elsewhere and that he couldn&#8217;t get it the attention it deserved into a different light – it is a series of essays on and dissections of individual works, but it doesn&#8217;t form a readable analysis or critique of Wolfe unless you are already so far in to the examination of Wolfe that you already know the existing arguments it is engaging with.</p>
<p id="comment-like-768" data-liked=comment-not-liked class="comment-likes comment-not-liked"><a href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/?like_comment=768&#038;_wpnonce=949e4ac6bf" class="comment-like-link needs-login" rel="nofollow" data-blog="85585660"><span>Like</span></a><span id="comment-like-count-768" class="comment-like-feedback">Like</span></p>
							</section><!-- .comment-content -->

				<div class="reply">
				<a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/?replytocom=768#respond" data-commentid="768" data-postid="2582" data-belowelement="comment-768" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to Mark" aria-label="Reply to Mark">Reply</a> <span>&darr;</span>				</div><!-- .reply -->
			</article><!-- #comment-## -->
				<ol class="children">
	<li class="comment even depth-2" id="li-comment-770">
		<article id="comment-770" class="comment">
			<header class="comment-meta comment-author vcard">
				<img referrerpolicy="no-referrer" alt='Marc Aramini&#039;s avatar' src='https://0.gravatar.com/avatar/9963e4f52d5a6dd855114c00e9034efa1e396548750d072f2d0565e7c1eaf1c7?s=44&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G' srcset='https://0.gravatar.com/avatar/9963e4f52d5a6dd855114c00e9034efa1e396548750d072f2d0565e7c1eaf1c7?s=44&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 1x, https://0.gravatar.com/avatar/9963e4f52d5a6dd855114c00e9034efa1e396548750d072f2d0565e7c1eaf1c7?s=66&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 1.5x, https://0.gravatar.com/avatar/9963e4f52d5a6dd855114c00e9034efa1e396548750d072f2d0565e7c1eaf1c7?s=88&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 2x, https://0.gravatar.com/avatar/9963e4f52d5a6dd855114c00e9034efa1e396548750d072f2d0565e7c1eaf1c7?s=132&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 3x, https://0.gravatar.com/avatar/9963e4f52d5a6dd855114c00e9034efa1e396548750d072f2d0565e7c1eaf1c7?s=176&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 4x' class='avatar avatar-44' height='44' width='44' loading='lazy' decoding='async' /><cite><b class="fn">Marc Aramini</b> </cite><a href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/#comment-770"><time datetime="2016-05-30T02:26:34+02:00">May 30, 2016 at 02:26</time></a>			</header><!-- .comment-meta -->

				
				
			<section class="comment-content comment">
				<p>Hi Mark. Thanks for reading it here and there. I do feel that opening with the essay on Fifth Head of Cerberus is a bit too esoteric for general readers, but I imagined that the individual stories would be a &#8220;complete&#8221; experience &#8211; read the story, read the analysis. If you are interested in a more general view on Wolfe, maybe the first video my youtube series might help. The sound quality on the first one is a bit dubious, but I found a better spot. After the first video, spoilers abound for whichever novel is being discussed. Here is the whole playlist. Thanks for looking it over.</p>
<p><span class="embed-youtube" style="text-align:center; display: block;"><iframe class="youtube-player" width="625" height="352" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed?version=3&#038;rel=1&#038;showsearch=0&#038;showinfo=1&#038;iv_load_policy=1&#038;fs=1&#038;hl=en&#038;autohide=2&#038;wmode=transparent&#038;listType=playlist&#038;list=PLzlbiFMwxeYCQwAzzyXpr3l3zAo4NBQ1c" allowfullscreen="true" style="border:0;" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-popups allow-presentation allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox"></iframe></span></p>
