		<p>Pingback: <a href="http://file770.com/?p=29223" class="url" rel="ugc external nofollow">Pixel Scroll 5/29/16 Hell Is Other Pixels | File 770</a> </p>
	</li><!-- #comment-## -->
	<li class="comment even thread-even depth-1" id="li-comment-775">
		<article id="comment-775" class="comment">
			<header class="comment-meta comment-author vcard">
				<img referrerpolicy="no-referrer" alt='Antonio&#039;s avatar' src='https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/160d3de47ed5a3402de766e8db1279ef2e75ddc77d2747fed3de9f89553698fb?s=44&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G' srcset='https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/160d3de47ed5a3402de766e8db1279ef2e75ddc77d2747fed3de9f89553698fb?s=44&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 1x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/160d3de47ed5a3402de766e8db1279ef2e75ddc77d2747fed3de9f89553698fb?s=66&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 1.5x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/160d3de47ed5a3402de766e8db1279ef2e75ddc77d2747fed3de9f89553698fb?s=88&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 2x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/160d3de47ed5a3402de766e8db1279ef2e75ddc77d2747fed3de9f89553698fb?s=132&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 3x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/160d3de47ed5a3402de766e8db1279ef2e75ddc77d2747fed3de9f89553698fb?s=176&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 4x' class='avatar avatar-44' height='44' width='44' loading='lazy' decoding='async' /><cite><b class="fn">Antonio</b> </cite><a href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/#comment-775"><time datetime="2016-05-30T03:51:02+02:00">May 30, 2016 at 03:51</time></a>			</header><!-- .comment-meta -->

				
				
			<section class="comment-content comment">
				<p>@Mark, I haven&#8217;t seen Aramini complain that he couldn&#8217;t get published elsewhere. I saw him fully acknowledging the quite niche nature of his book, but pointing out that it still should deserve at least a &#8216;thanks, but&#8230;&#8217; from the folks he&#8217;s showed it to.</p>
<p>I get what you mean both about the book essentially consiring of outright discussions of specific points in each story with little or no introduction, as well as not having sections devoted to the discussion of Gebe Wolfe&#8217;s work as a whole. That is true, but it&#8217;s just the type of work that it is &#8211; an attempt to glean all analyzable commonalities from each of the texts &#8211; and building a perspective of the whole as appropriate &#8211; so that later on critiques of Wolfe may be more informed. It&#8217;s not meant as a definite word on Wolfe, it&#8217;s meant as a stepping stone for many other words. Even so, for the Wolfe fan it&#8217;s already a treasure trove. But it sure makes little sense to read any part of it unless you&#8217;ve read the ext it refers to and are looking for more intellectual stimulation. In that regard, it isn&#8217;t soemthing that a general sf fan with no experience with Wolfe should expect to make much sense of.</p>
<p id="comment-like-775" data-liked=comment-not-liked class="comment-likes comment-not-liked"><a href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/?like_comment=775&#038;_wpnonce=f47df1876d" class="comment-like-link needs-login" rel="nofollow" data-blog="85585660"><span>Like</span></a><span id="comment-like-count-775" class="comment-like-feedback">Like</span></p>
							</section><!-- .comment-content -->

				<div class="reply">
				<a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/?replytocom=775#respond" data-commentid="775" data-postid="2582" data-belowelement="comment-775" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to Antonio" aria-label="Reply to Antonio">Reply</a> <span>&darr;</span>				</div><!-- .reply -->
			</article><!-- #comment-## -->
				<ol class="children">
	<li class="comment byuser comment-author-markhepworthuk odd alt depth-2" id="li-comment-784">
		<article id="comment-784" class="comment">
			<header class="comment-meta comment-author vcard">
				<img referrerpolicy="no-referrer" alt='Mark Hepworth&#039;s avatar' src='https://2.gravatar.com/avatar/bc2b6cf4d1b82d574c2b84659612a1c7a86436580c6fe0c63091958b6132321a?s=44&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G' srcset='https://2.gravatar.com/avatar/bc2b6cf4d1b82d574c2b84659612a1c7a86436580c6fe0c63091958b6132321a?s=44&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 1x, https://2.gravatar.com/avatar/bc2b6cf4d1b82d574c2b84659612a1c7a86436580c6fe0c63091958b6132321a?s=66&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 1.5x, https://2.gravatar.com/avatar/bc2b6cf4d1b82d574c2b84659612a1c7a86436580c6fe0c63091958b6132321a?s=88&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 2x, https://2.gravatar.com/avatar/bc2b6cf4d1b82d574c2b84659612a1c7a86436580c6fe0c63091958b6132321a?s=132&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 3x, https://2.gravatar.com/avatar/bc2b6cf4d1b82d574c2b84659612a1c7a86436580c6fe0c63091958b6132321a?s=176&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 4x' class='avatar avatar-44' height='44' width='44' loading='lazy' decoding='async' /><cite><b class="fn"><a href="http://sfmmxv.wordpress.com" class="url" rel="ugc external nofollow">Mark</a></b> </cite><a href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/#comment-784"><time datetime="2016-05-30T11:29:27+02:00">May 30, 2016 at 11:29</time></a>			</header><!-- .comment-meta -->

				
				
			<section class="comment-content comment">
				<p>Antonio,</p>
<p>Aramini said in the interview “I still feel that my work deserved better than to be ignored by the many venues I attempted to send it to” and also commented on the issue<a href="http://file770.com/?p=28616&amp;cpage=4#comment-424205" rel="nofollow"> here</a>.</p>
<p>We are in agreement on the nature of the work, and that it is not necessarily a criticism, just the nature of what Aramini has written. However, that doesn&#8217;t prevent it being an issue that would make it difficult to get it published, and make it unlikely to garner awards.</p>
<p id="comment-like-784" data-liked=comment-not-liked class="comment-likes comment-not-liked"><a href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/?like_comment=784&#038;_wpnonce=0827ccbc3a" class="comment-like-link needs-login" rel="nofollow" data-blog="85585660"><span>Like</span></a><span id="comment-like-count-784" class="comment-like-feedback">Like</span></p>
							</section><!-- .comment-content -->

