				<img referrerpolicy="no-referrer" alt='Hoof &amp; Hide&#039;s avatar' src='https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/d2402a4dbdf7019d0e9cf74ae0570eea8c57e3933c6a69cd64eb2d680e23fed7?s=44&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G' srcset='https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/d2402a4dbdf7019d0e9cf74ae0570eea8c57e3933c6a69cd64eb2d680e23fed7?s=44&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 1x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/d2402a4dbdf7019d0e9cf74ae0570eea8c57e3933c6a69cd64eb2d680e23fed7?s=66&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 1.5x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/d2402a4dbdf7019d0e9cf74ae0570eea8c57e3933c6a69cd64eb2d680e23fed7?s=88&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 2x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/d2402a4dbdf7019d0e9cf74ae0570eea8c57e3933c6a69cd64eb2d680e23fed7?s=132&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 3x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/d2402a4dbdf7019d0e9cf74ae0570eea8c57e3933c6a69cd64eb2d680e23fed7?s=176&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 4x' class='avatar avatar-44' height='44' width='44' loading='lazy' decoding='async' /><cite><b class="fn"><a href="http://www.hoofandhide.com" class="url" rel="ugc external nofollow">mraf</a></b> </cite><a href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/#comment-789"><time datetime="2016-05-30T13:49:44+02:00">May 30, 2016 at 13:49</time></a>			</header><!-- .comment-meta -->

				
				
			<section class="comment-content comment">
				<p>Reblogged this on <a href="https://hoofandhide.wordpress.com/2016/05/30/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/" rel="nofollow">Hoof&amp;Hide</a> and commented:<br />
I thoroughly enjoyed this interview with Marc Aramini and can&#8217;t wait to get my hands on a hard copy of his book (and volume 2 for that matter. Whether you&#8217;ve read Gene Wolfe or not this interview is certainly worth a few moments of your time.</p>
<p id="comment-like-789" data-liked=comment-not-liked class="comment-likes comment-not-liked"><a href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/?like_comment=789&#038;_wpnonce=2b4fa97a62" class="comment-like-link needs-login" rel="nofollow" data-blog="85585660"><span>Like</span></a><span id="comment-like-count-789" class="comment-like-feedback">Liked by <a href="#" class="view-likers" data-like-count="1">1 person</a></span></p>
							</section><!-- .comment-content -->

				<div class="reply">
				<a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/?replytocom=789#respond" data-commentid="789" data-postid="2582" data-belowelement="comment-789" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to mraf" aria-label="Reply to mraf">Reply</a> <span>&darr;</span>				</div><!-- .reply -->
			</article><!-- #comment-## -->
				</li><!-- #comment-## -->
	<li class="comment byuser comment-author-stevejwright odd alt thread-even depth-1" id="li-comment-815">
		<article id="comment-815" class="comment">
			<header class="comment-meta comment-author vcard">
				<img referrerpolicy="no-referrer" alt='stevejwright&#039;s avatar' src='https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/1217a1e65432ca639c5df8e8291a5226f467592f515814831a2e59082997f5a3?s=44&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G' srcset='https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/1217a1e65432ca639c5df8e8291a5226f467592f515814831a2e59082997f5a3?s=44&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 1x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/1217a1e65432ca639c5df8e8291a5226f467592f515814831a2e59082997f5a3?s=66&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 1.5x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/1217a1e65432ca639c5df8e8291a5226f467592f515814831a2e59082997f5a3?s=88&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 2x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/1217a1e65432ca639c5df8e8291a5226f467592f515814831a2e59082997f5a3?s=132&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 3x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/1217a1e65432ca639c5df8e8291a5226f467592f515814831a2e59082997f5a3?s=176&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 4x' class='avatar avatar-44' height='44' width='44' loading='lazy' decoding='async' /><cite><b class="fn"><a href="http://stevejwright.wordpress.com" class="url" rel="ugc external nofollow">stevejwright</a></b> </cite><a href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/#comment-815"><time datetime="2016-05-31T11:53:47+02:00">May 31, 2016 at 11:53</time></a>			</header><!-- .comment-meta -->

				
				
			<section class="comment-content comment">
				<p>I&#8217;ve read Wolfe.  I&#8217;ve been a fan since &#8220;The Fifth Head of Cerberus&#8221;, and I intend to have my much-thumbed copy of that by my side when I read Aramini &#8211; along with equally-thumbed copies of the New Sun books, &#8220;The Island of Doctor Death and Other Stories and Other Stories&#8221;, &#8220;Book of Days&#8221;, and even &#8220;Operation Ares&#8221;.  </p>
<p>Wolfe is a dense, tricky, allusive writer and there&#8217;s a lot to say about him.  Of course, a lot has already been said &#8211; there are several volumes of Wolfe scholarship out there, and have been for some time (most, if not all, from rather more, umm, well-regarded publishing houses.)  It is true that it&#8217;s hard to get a book on Wolfe published, but only in the sense that it&#8217;s hard to get any book published.  (Trust me on this, I know, from bitter experience.)</p>
<p>But I&#8217;m going to read Aramini&#8217;s stuff before I judge it.</p>
<p id="comment-like-815" data-liked=comment-not-liked class="comment-likes comment-not-liked"><a href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/?like_comment=815&#038;_wpnonce=54ecf002f3" class="comment-like-link needs-login" rel="nofollow" data-blog="85585660"><span>Like</span></a><span id="comment-like-count-815" class="comment-like-feedback">Like</span></p>
							</section><!-- .comment-content -->

				<div class="reply">
				<a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/?replytocom=815#respond" data-commentid="815" data-postid="2582" data-belowelement="comment-815" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to stevejwright" aria-label="Reply to stevejwright">Reply</a> <span>&darr;</span>				</div><!-- .reply -->
			</article><!-- #comment-## -->
				</li><!-- #comment-## -->
	<li class="comment byuser comment-author-lurkertype even thread-odd thread-alt depth-1" id="li-comment-863">
		<article id="comment-863" class="comment">
			<header class="comment-meta comment-author vcard">
				<img referrerpolicy="no-referrer" alt='Lurkertype&#039;s avatar' src='https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/77b2125d28e0eefbfe779adf4968350f61bd9117e626a3433ac08ea56db0bc63?s=44&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G' srcset='https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/77b2125d28e0eefbfe779adf4968350f61bd9117e626a3433ac08ea56db0bc63?s=44&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 1x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/77b2125d28e0eefbfe779adf4968350f61bd9117e626a3433ac08ea56db0bc63?s=66&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 1.5x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/77b2125d28e0eefbfe779adf4968350f61bd9117e626a3433ac08ea56db0bc63?s=88&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 2x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/77b2125d28e0eefbfe779adf4968350f61bd9117e626a3433ac08ea56db0bc63?s=132&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 3x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/77b2125d28e0eefbfe779adf4968350f61bd9117e626a3433ac08ea56db0bc63?s=176&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 4x' class='avatar avatar-44' height='44' width='44' loading='lazy' decoding='async' /><cite><b class="fn"><a href="http://lurkertype.wordpress.com" class="url" rel="ugc external nofollow">Lurkertype</a></b> </cite><a href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/#comment-863"><time datetime="2016-06-03T04:25:42+02:00">June 3, 2016 at 04:25</time></a>			</header><!-- .comment-meta -->

				
				
			<section class="comment-content comment">
				<p>While it sounds like a fine book and certainly a labor of love, I don&#8217;t think it would have gotten onto the Hugo ballot honestly. Hugos cover the wide general range of SFnal stuff, and this is very, very niche. Deeply scholarly books that don&#8217;t draw overall conclusions and which can&#8217;t be understood without knowing what they&#8217;re in conversation with aren&#8217;t crowd-pleasers. Regardless of quality, it&#8217;s not the sort of book that makes it to the ballot in years that don&#8217;t have one guy determined to either destroy the award or use it to market his own stuff. </p>
<p>This is not to say that Mr. Aramini hasn&#8217;t done a great work of scholarship, just that it wouldn&#8217;t have made the final list if not for the slating. Not his fault, but there it is.</p>
<p id="comment-like-863" data-liked=comment-not-liked class="comment-likes comment-not-liked"><a href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/?like_comment=863&#038;_wpnonce=634fadcf4d" class="comment-like-link needs-login" rel="nofollow" data-blog="85585660"><span>Like</span></a><span id="comment-like-count-863" class="comment-like-feedback">Liked by <a href="#" class="view-likers" data-like-count="1">1 person</a></span></p>
							</section><!-- .comment-content -->

				<div class="reply">
				<a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/?replytocom=863#respond" data-commentid="863" data-postid="2582" data-belowelement="comment-863" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to Lurkertype" aria-label="Reply to Lurkertype">Reply</a> <span>&darr;</span>				</div><!-- .reply -->
			</article><!-- #comment-## -->
				<ol class="children">
	<li class="comment odd alt depth-2" id="li-comment-866">
		<article id="comment-866" class="comment">
			<header class="comment-meta comment-author vcard">
				<img referrerpolicy="no-referrer" alt='Marc Aramini&#039;s avatar' src='https://0.gravatar.com/avatar/9963e4f52d5a6dd855114c00e9034efa1e396548750d072f2d0565e7c1eaf1c7?s=44&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G' srcset='https://0.gravatar.com/avatar/9963e4f52d5a6dd855114c00e9034efa1e396548750d072f2d0565e7c1eaf1c7?s=44&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 1x, https://0.gravatar.com/avatar/9963e4f52d5a6dd855114c00e9034efa1e396548750d072f2d0565e7c1eaf1c7?s=66&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 1.5x, https://0.gravatar.com/avatar/9963e4f52d5a6dd855114c00e9034efa1e396548750d072f2d0565e7c1eaf1c7?s=88&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 2x, https://0.gravatar.com/avatar/9963e4f52d5a6dd855114c00e9034efa1e396548750d072f2d0565e7c1eaf1c7?s=132&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 3x, https://0.gravatar.com/avatar/9963e4f52d5a6dd855114c00e9034efa1e396548750d072f2d0565e7c1eaf1c7?s=176&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 4x' class='avatar avatar-44' height='44' width='44' loading='lazy' decoding='async' /><cite><b class="fn">Marc Aramini</b> </cite><a href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/#comment-866"><time datetime="2016-06-03T12:30:53+02:00">June 3, 2016 at 12:30</time></a>			</header><!-- .comment-meta -->

				
				
			<section class="comment-content comment">
				<p>Certainly I intended it to be a general reference book to aid general readers. For example, if you are confused by the end of The Doctor of Death Island, I do all of the Dickens research and lay out the most thematically apt conclusion so you don&#8217;t have to. Whether I succeeded in making it accessible to all fans or not, that was my intention, not to engage scholars. I drew many, many conclusions about individual stories, answering &#8220;what the heck happened here?&#8221; See &#8220;melting,&#8221; &#8220;the changeling,&#8221; &#8220;suzanne delage,&#8221; &#8220;seven American nights,&#8221; etc. </p>
<p>Now whether it woild have ever been on the Hugo ballot , a popularity award, is another story. But it was designed as a general reference for any reader of Wolfe nd I feel the characterizatiom above is not accurate regarding the short stories.</p>
<p id="comment-like-866" data-liked=comment-not-liked class="comment-likes comment-not-liked"><a href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/?like_comment=866&#038;_wpnonce=ebb1ad79f3" class="comment-like-link needs-login" rel="nofollow" data-blog="85585660"><span>Like</span></a><span id="comment-like-count-866" class="comment-like-feedback">Like</span></p>
							</section><!-- .comment-content -->

				<div class="reply">
				<a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/?replytocom=866#respond" data-commentid="866" data-postid="2582" data-belowelement="comment-866" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to Marc Aramini" aria-label="Reply to Marc Aramini">Reply</a> <span>&darr;</span>				</div><!-- .reply -->
			</article><!-- #comment-## -->
				</li><!-- #comment-## -->
</ol><!-- .children -->
</li><!-- #comment-## -->
	<li class="comment byuser comment-author-aaronsingleton even thread-even depth-1" id="li-comment-867">
		<article id="comment-867" class="comment">
			<header class="comment-meta comment-author vcard">
				<img referrerpolicy="no-referrer" alt='aaronsingleton&#039;s avatar' src='https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/44f57109b3ad77a820d32d70aaf2106e610bc035680977212b8ebc595f27e2c2?s=44&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G' srcset='https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/44f57109b3ad77a820d32d70aaf2106e610bc035680977212b8ebc595f27e2c2?s=44&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 1x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/44f57109b3ad77a820d32d70aaf2106e610bc035680977212b8ebc595f27e2c2?s=66&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 1.5x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/44f57109b3ad77a820d32d70aaf2106e610bc035680977212b8ebc595f27e2c2?s=88&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 2x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/44f57109b3ad77a820d32d70aaf2106e610bc035680977212b8ebc595f27e2c2?s=132&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 3x, https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/44f57109b3ad77a820d32d70aaf2106e610bc035680977212b8ebc595f27e2c2?s=176&#038;d=identicon&#038;r=G 4x' class='avatar avatar-44' height='44' width='44' loading='lazy' decoding='async' /><cite><b class="fn"><a href="http://infernalmachina.wordpress.com" class="url" rel="ugc external nofollow">aaronsingleton</a></b> </cite><a href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/#comment-867"><time datetime="2016-06-03T22:40:59+02:00">June 3, 2016 at 22:40</time></a>			</header><!-- .comment-meta -->

				
				
			<section class="comment-content comment">
				<p>I bought Aramini&#8217;s book as soon as I saw it on Amazon. It deserves, in my opinion, to be held in the same regard as Andre-Driussi&#8217;s Lexicon Urthus. I have told Marc personally that I enjoyed his work almost as much as reading Wolfe himself. Thanks again Marc.</p>
<p id="comment-like-867" data-liked=comment-not-liked class="comment-likes comment-not-liked"><a href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/?like_comment=867&#038;_wpnonce=ad5d0ebd32" class="comment-like-link needs-login" rel="nofollow" data-blog="85585660"><span>Like</span></a><span id="comment-like-count-867" class="comment-like-feedback">Like</span></p>
							</section><!-- .comment-content -->

				<div class="reply">
				<a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="https://sfkittens.wordpress.com/2016/05/29/gene-wolfe-for-n00bs-an-interview-with-marc-aramini/?replytocom=867#respond" data-commentid="867" data-postid="2582" data-belowelement="comment-867" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to aaronsingleton" aria-label="Reply to aaronsingleton">Reply</a> <span>&darr;</span>				</div><!-- .reply -->
